        "id": "ch12_3_6-1",
        "text": "Secure Shell (SSH) remoting\nThe SSH protocol is a cryptographic protocol that supports secure network services over an unsecured\nnetwork. It is cross-platform and works on both Windows and Linux/Mac systems. It relies on public\nkey cryptography; we need to generate a key pair and pass the public key to the system we want\nto remote to. When we subsequently open a session, we specify the path to the private key on our\nmachine, and SSH verifies that the public key on the remote machine is part of a pair with the local\nprivate key. At no point is the private key passed over the network. While setup is quite complex,\nusing SSH once it is set up is very easy.",
